<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Cardona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardona">Cardona</a> was a Catalan noble family named after the castle and salt mountain of Cardona in central Catalonia. Viscounts from the 10th century, they became counts in 1375 and dukes in 1491, ranking among the greatest lords of the Crown of Aragon. After the defeat of the last count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallars">Pallars</a> Sobirà, Ferdinand II granted them his confiscated lands as the Marquisate of Pallars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-cardona.jpg" alt="House of Cardona" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heralder · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_House_of_Folch,_Dukes_of_Cardona.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
